  "term": "spontaneous discharge",
  "definition": "Spontaneous discharge is the baseline firing activity of neurons that occurs without an added stimulus. In this source, it refers to the rate at which locus coeruleus neurons fire on their own, which was found to increase during opiate withdrawal.",
